    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You sort workplace messages from employees into one intent.\nReply only in the required format.\n\nmulti = the message contains TWO OR MORE separate requests that need different actions, for example 'refund ORD-1004 and add a task to follow up', 'where is ORD-1002 and how many casual leaves do I get', 'add a task and show revenue by region'. A single request, even a long one, is never multi. A message with one request that has a reason or detail attached is not multi.\npolicy = questions about leave entitlements, holidays and the general HR handbook.\nhiring = questions about candidates, resumes, interviews, job roles.\nops = adding, updating or asking about tasks, deadlines or daily updates.\nanalytics = questions about sales data or numbers: revenue, profit, cost, units, orders, regions, products, channels, trends, top or bottom performers, charts or comparisons of sales.\nsupport = a request to DO something with an order: asking for a refund, a return, or the status or location of an order, usually mentioning an order ID like ORD-1001. Any message that asks for a refund is support, even if it mentions a reason.\naudit = ONLY a question about what the bots already did: the history, audit trail or replay of past actions, or why a past decision was made. Examples: 'show history for ORD-1004', 'why was ORD-1004 refunded', 'replay the last 5 actions', 'what did the bots do recently'. A request to perform an action is never audit.\nknowledge = questions about company documents other than leave: IT security rules (passwords, MFA, devices, phishing), expense claims and travel limits, onboarding and probation, working hours and remote work or hybrid rules, and product plans, pricing, trials, general refund policy, support and compliance (general policy questions that are not about a specific order).\nother = anything else, including greetings.\n\nGive a confidence from 0 to 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
